-- title:
--   Recognition of O[[U,V]]/(UV-varpi) at a crossing point
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, and let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible. Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local $O$-algebra which is adically complete for its maximal ideal, and assume that the composite of the structure map $O \to R$ with the residue map $R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ is surjective, i.e. $O$ already surjects onto the residue field of $R$. Suppose given $u, v \in R$ with $u v = \varpi \cdot 1_R$ (the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map) and such that $$\mathfrak m_R = \mathfrak m_O R + (u,v) + \mathfrak m_R^2,$$ the sum in the lattice of ideals of the image ideal of $\mathfrak m_O$, the ideal generated by $u$ and $v$, and the square of $\mathfrak m_R$; suppose further that the Krull dimension of $R$ is at least $2$. Then the type of $O$-algebra isomorphisms from $R$ to $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,O$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \varpi$, that is to $O[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi)$, is nonempty.
--
--   This is the recognition principle for an ordinary double point (a crossing) over a discrete valuation ring: a complete Noetherian local $O$-algebra with residue field that of $O$, whose cotangent space is spanned by two elements with product a uniformiser, and of dimension at least two, is $O[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi)$. It feeds the analysis of the local structure of the deformation rings arising in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, where a prorepresenting ring is shown to be either a power series ring or such a crossing model.
